arter kits were distributed.\n24: - 36 Braille outreach flyers were printed for accessible pickup locations.\n25: - 18 volunteer setup shifts were completed.\n\n(End of file - total 25 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"## Final Closeout Summary\n\nThe correct reimbursement cap for closeout is `$1,600.00`, using `03_award_update_2026-05-22.md` as the controlling source. That award update is newer than `02_award_letter_2026-04-15.md`, and the local instructions require using the newest dated award document when award-cap sources conflict.\n\nThe corrected reimbursable total is `$1,588.00`, leaving `$12.00` remaining under the cap.\n\nUseful prior work preserved:\n\n- The approval of `G-001` for garden supplies.\n- The approval of `G-003` for accessibility printing.\n- The rejection of `G-004` for staff gifts.\n- The outcome facts that 140 seedling starter kits were distributed and 36 Braille outreach flyers were printed.\n\nWrong prior work corrected:\n\n- The cap was updated from the superseded `$2,000.00` original award letter to the correct `$1,600.00` award update.\n- `G-002` was reduced from `$145.00` to `$120.00` because volunteer refreshments are capped at `$120.00`.\n- `G-005` was changed from approved to rejected because public outreach printing is not an eligible category under the current rules and the expense also lacks the required receipt for an amount over `$75.00`.\n- The omitted `G-006` postage expense was added and approved at `$68.00` because public outreach postage is eligible and no receipt is required for this amount with a ledger note.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/final_closeout_summary.md","text":"## Final Closeout Summary\n\nThe correct reimbursement cap for closeout is `$1,600.00`, using `03_award_update_2026-05-22.md` as the controlling source. That award update is newer than `02_award_letter_2026-04-15.md`, and the local ins